# =============================================================================
# THIS PROJECT HAS NO CONTAINER, AND THIS FILE IS AN EXPLANATION, NOT A BUILD.
# =============================================================================
#
# The template ships a Dockerfile.example because most projects deploy something.
# This one does not. Kept rather than deleted, because "we have no container"
# and "nobody thought about packaging" look identical from outside.
#
# WHY THERE IS NOTHING TO CONTAINERISE
#
#   ADR-002   The kit ships no executable code. There is no process, no server,
#             no entrypoint - nothing a container would start.
#   CON-001   It is a Claude Code plugin: Markdown files installed into a
#             repository by the host's own mechanism.
#   CON-003   No network calls at run time. Nothing to expose, nothing to reach.
#   CON-006   No runtime, no package manager, no dependency to install.
#
#   The unit of distribution is a PLUGIN VERSION on a marketplace, not an image
#   on a registry. See 07-ops/01-deployment/deployment-plan.md.
#
# THE ONE PLACE A CONTAINER *IS* USED
#
#   CI. The gate and the scheduled install test run somewhere, and that somewhere
#   is whatever the chosen provider gives us. That belongs to cicd-pipeline.md,
#   not here - it is infrastructure for CHECKING the kit, never for SHIPPING it.
#
#   FF-009 asserts the published payload contains zero files that are not Markdown
#   or the plugin manifest. A Dockerfile inside the payload would fail that check,
#   correctly.
#
# IF YOU ARE ABOUT TO WRITE A REAL DOCKERFILE HERE, STOP.
#
#   A container implies a process, which implies a runtime, which supersedes
#   ADR-002. Write the superseding ADR first; the Dockerfile follows from that
#   decision rather than leading it.
#
#   The likely honest reason you are here is that you want a reproducible
#   environment for CI. That is cicd-pipeline.md's job, and it does not need this
#   file to exist.
#
# See also:
#   01-docs/05-architecture/architecture-decisions/ADR-002-instructions-only-no-runtime.md
#   07-ops/01-deployment/deployment-plan.md
#   .env.example                                     (empty, for the same reason)
